Executing : cfg_set_device_property -help
H: cfg_set_device_property : set device properties (Version 2022.2-SP6.4 build 146967)
    [ -help  ]
        Turn on to print this message
    [ -device_index integer_number ]
        Specify target device's index
    [ -program string ]
        Specify programmed value of program properties.   ---Hexadecimal Number.
          Bit0: Enable WakeDown Reconfigure. 
          Bit1: Enable ISC Reconfigure.      
          Bit2: Enable HighZDis Reconfigure. 
          If a bit is setting 1,it means that this function is valid.
          Such as, if Bit0 and Bit1 is setting 1, the value of program properties is 3.
          Notice: Bit1 and Bit2 can not be set to 1 at the same time for specific series device.
    [ -readback string ]
        Specify programmed value of read back properties.   ---Hexadecimal Number.
          Bit0: Enable WakeDown Read Back. 
          Bit1: Enable ISC Read Back.      
          Bit2: Enable HighZDis Read Back. 
          If a bit is setting 1,it means that this function is valid.
          Such as, if Bit0 and Bit2 is setting 1, the value of read back properties is 5.
          Notice: Bit1 and Bit2 can not be set to 1 at the same time for specific series device.
    [ -eflash string ]
        Specify programmed value of embed flash properties.   ---Hexadecimal Number.
          Bit0: Enable Erase before Program Embed Flash.
          Bit1: Enable Verify after Program Embed Flash.
          Bit2: Enable Erase Entire Embed Flash.
          Bit3: Enable Reset FPGA after Erase Embed Flash.
          Bit4: Enable Reset FPGA after Program Embed Flash.
          Bit5: Enable Reset FPGA after Program Feature Control.
          Bit6: Enable Program Feature Control after Program EFlash.
          Bit7: Enable Program Feature Control before Program CRAM.
          Bit19-Bit8 :  Embed Flash Start Page Index(Unit: 256Byte).   total pages:332   ---Decimal Number
          Bit31-Bit20:  Embed Flash Tail  Page Index(Unit: 256Byte).   total pages:332   ---Decimal Number
          Bit51-Bit32:  Embed Flash Read  Back Size(Unit: Byte).   ---Hexadecimal Number.
          If a bit is setting 1,it means that this function is valid.
          Such as, if only Bit0 and Bit5 is setting 1, the value of embed flash properties is 21.
          The use of the tcl command: cfg_set_device_property -device_index 0 -program 3 -readback 5 -eflash 21.
          Notice: the arguments program and eflash are hexadecimal number and optional.


